 "notes": {
  "sha512": "Until 4b9aa7d hxmc native and wasm computed wrong SHA-512 digests after minor collections: Bytes.alloc did not zero its bytes (hxc's rt_alloc did), and the crypto library's Sha512 pads its last block with them, so a nursery reused after a collection left dead objects' bytes in it. Fixed (Bytes.alloc zeroed); the three hxmc sha512 rows were re-measured on 2026-10-15 and their digests match every other target. The --check programs of every case were re-run for the three hxmc targets after the fix: all outputs equal to hxc's.",
  "json": "digests equal on every target; the printed float format differs (HL: -3e-07, JVM: -3.0E-7, 1.0E21, 3.0073737643E10): Std.string of Float is target-dependent",
  "formatter_noio": "formatted text identical (dumped and compared for JS and JVM); the JVM's haxe.crypto.Sha256 of the non-ASCII text differs from the other targets' (the generic Sha256 uses s.length * 8 as the bit length; the JVM's agrees with sha256sum of the UTF-8 bytes)",
  "wasm failures": "none; wasmtime needs PWD without symbolic links to absolute paths (fixed in the harness: the case directory is resolved)"
 }
